# docker/.dockerignore
#
# !!! THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE - IT HAS NO EFFECT WHERE IT SITS !!!
#
# The Docker daemon always reads the ignore file from the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT.
# The agri build uses the repository root as context:
#
#     docker build --file docker/Dockerfile --target production -t agri-platform:latest .
#
# so the daemon looks for <repo-root>/.dockerignore and never sees this file.
# Creating <repo-root>/.dockerignore was outside this change-set's write scope
# (docker/ + .github/ only). The same content is therefore:
#   * reproduced verbatim in the header comment of docker/Dockerfile,
#   * kept ready-to-paste in .github/DOCKERIGNORE.md,
#   * documented in docker/README.md.
#
# ACTION REQUIRED (repo owner): copy this file to <repo-root>/.dockerignore.
# Until then builds are CORRECT but slower (the whole working tree, including
# data/raw imagery and .venv, is sent to the daemon).
#
# docker/Dockerfile only uses explicit, narrow COPY statements, so no ignored
# path above can leak into an image layer regardless of this file.

# --- vcs / ci / tooling ------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- python virtualenvs & caches --------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage*.xml
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- data, models, reports: mounted at run time, never baked -----------------
data/
models/
reports/
mlruns/
mlartifacts/

# --- docs / dev-only trees (not needed to build or run the image) -----------
docs/
notebooks/
scripts/
tests/
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- secrets: never send them to the daemon ---------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- os / editor noise ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
